## Now
- Current udm-rest-api container: installs debian packages
    - has to fake various scripts
    - post install patches
    - dpkg --force-depends
- long feedback loop
    - no easy possibility for developers to test their changes in nubus for kubernetes
    - container broke after a base image update, investigating failing tests due to upstream changes
    - releasing new features in nubus for kubernetes in one sprint is hard due to packages needing to be released first

## What I built
- source based, multi-stage Dockerfile in the UCS repo
- uv workspace, resolving all internal dependencies through the workspace
- added a `pyproject.toml` to internal dependencies, allowing them to get resolved from the uv workspace
- POC integration into the udm-rest-api helm chart

## Does it work?
- Integrated into the udm-rest-api helm chart with minimal changes
- Tested against nubus for kubernetes end-to-end tests
    - 3 initial failed tests
        - 2 flaky
        - 1 test caught during testing. Present in both containers, would've surfaced in the old one on the next base-image rebuild.
- docker compose based tests from the nubus for kubernetes repo in CI

## Metrics

|                 | Debian based | Source based                                             |
| --------------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| Image Size      | 644 MB       | 364 MB                                                   |
| SBOM components | 284          | 196 (further reduction possible with smaller base-image) |
| Dockerfile size | 268 lines    | ~76 lines                                                |
Plus:
- No faked postinst scripts
- No dpkg force-depends

## Feedback loop
- source based container means developers can run full e2e against their own changes in nubus for kubernetes
- one real bug already found during the spike.
    - appears in both containers, however was not found during development
    - would cost a lot of time during a base image update
    - could've been caught earlier
- release with more confidence: test against both platforms at the same time
## What I also did
- Moving the udm-rest-api to a source buildable container required to make the UCS repo more like a real python monorepo
- Created `pyproject.toml` for various projects which are needed by the udm-rest-api
    - partly new, written from scratch
    - partly migrated `setup.py`s
- create a uv workspace with the dependencies declared
    - gives up monorepo atomicity for all UCS packages
    - workspace can declare dependency versions
- declared cross project internal dependencies in pyproject.toml
    - installing the udm-rest-api is a `uv-sync` in the dockerfile
    - enable modern PEP517 builds

## More work needed
- debian packages which had a pyproject.toml added need some work
    - for simple projects: just an additional flag in `debian/rules`
    - some more complicated projects may need to be restructured a bit, e.g. when one src tree builds multiple debian python packages.
    - polish pyproject.toml in various projects (e.g. version information)
- Dockerfile improvements
    - current runs as root
    - Translations files missing (can be solved via setup.py similar to UMC)

## How to continue from here:
1. Fix pyproject.toml in UCS repo.
    - proper versoning
    - make all debian packages build
    - make sure there's no changes in debian packages
2. polish Dockerfile
3. split up udm-rest-api repo
    * move helm chart into ums-stack
    * consolidate extra containers
4. integrate into nubus-helm

- at some point: local dev env with a proper venv and proper LSP support (currently blocked by native deps)

